/* 段落记忆 · 词层 4 · 子块 d：词头 → {tw:[关系词,关系类型], en, zh} */
window.APP_MERGE_NET(4,{"sub":"d","par":{"terminal":{"tw":[["term",4],["end",0],["finish",3],["station",2],["intermediate",1],["transit",6],["final",0],["tip",3],["contact",2],["rail",6],["last",0]],"en":"On the last evening of our trip we reached the bus terminal just before the rain. The clerk at the station told us our ticket was for an intermediate stop, not the final one. I had to keep in contact with the driver, who knew the rail line well and had worked on it for years. During the transit we passed an old building whose roof had lost its tip in a storm. The term of our ticket would end at midnight, so we had to finish the ride in one go. My sister said this was the last leg of the journey, and no timetable could help us after that. When we stepped out at the end of the line, the sky had cleared.","zh":"出门的最后一个傍晚，我们赶在雨前到了长途汽车终点站。售票窗口的人说，我们的票只到中途一站，并不是最后一站。我只好一直跟司机保持联系，他对那条铁路线很熟，在上面干了多年。路上经过一栋老房子，屋顶的一角被大风刮掉了。票的有效期到午夜就结束，所以我们得一口气坐完这段。姐姐说这已是旅程的最后一段，再晚什么时刻表都帮不上忙。等我们在线路尽头下车时，天已经放晴了。"},"romance":{"tw":[["romantic",4],["court",0],["chase",3],["act",2],["tale",6],["flirt",0],["display",3],["lie",2],["novel",6],["mash",0]],"en":"My cousin likes to tell a tale about her parents' long romance. They met at a village fair, where he would flirt with her over a stall of fruit. She says he was never romantic in the usual way; he showed his feelings through small acts of help. In the first week he would chase her little brother around the field and then lie on the grass, laughing. Their story was later made into a short novel, a soft display of young love. He would court her for two winters before she said yes. Now the two of them mash potatoes together in the same kitchen.","zh":"我表姐爱讲她父母那段漫长恋爱的故事。他们是在村里的集市上认识的，他在水果摊前跟她搭话。她说他从不是那种浪漫的人，是靠一件件小事的帮忙来表达心意。头一个星期，他追着她弟弟在田里跑，然后躺在草地上笑。他们的故事后来被写成了一部短篇小说，是年轻爱情一种温和的展现。他求了她两个冬天，她才答应。如今两个人在同一个厨房里一起捣土豆泥。"},"sketch":{"tw":[["sketchy",4],["study",0],["design",3],["draw",2],["comic",6],["outline",0],["draft",3],["describe",2],["parody",6],["resume",0]],"en":"In art class our teacher asked us to draw a quick sketch of the old bridge. First she told us to study the line of the roof and then to describe it in a single sentence. My first draft was only an outline, and the details were still sketchy. A boy next to me made a comic version of the same view, a friendly parody of the real thing. In the afternoon the teacher began to design a poster for the school show. She said we could resume the work after lunch and hand it in on Friday. Nobody expected the fastest hand to win the prize.","zh":"美术课上，老师让我们给那座老桥画一张速写。她先让我们观察屋顶的线条，再用一句话把它描述出来。我的第一稿只是一圈轮廓，细节还很粗糙。我旁边一个男生把同一个景画成了漫画，算是善意地戏仿实物。下午老师开始为学校的演出设计一张海报。她说午饭之后可以接着画，周五交。谁也没想到，画得最快的那个人会得奖。"},"terminate":{"tw":[["terminus",4],["end",0],["break",3],["change",2],["consent",6],["finish",3],["close",3],["remove",2],["discontinue",6],["fire",0]],"en":"Last month the manager decided to terminate the contract of a worker who often came late. Before that, the company had to give him a chance to change his habits. He did not consent to the new terms, so the office chose to discontinue the old agreement. At the terminus of the bus line he stood with a box of tools in his arms. He had to remove them from the shelf and close the door of the small workshop. During the break some of us talked about him; for him the work would come to an end that day. That was not a happy finish, and a fire in the yard the next night made the week stranger still.","zh":"上个月，经理决定终止一个总迟到的工人的合同。在那之前，公司得先给他一个改掉习惯的机会。他不肯接受新条款，办公室便选择中止那份旧协议。他抱着一箱工具，站在公交线路的终点站上。他得把工具从架子上取下来，再把小作坊的门关上。工间休息时我们几个聊起他；对他来说，那份活计那天就算到头了。这个收场并不痛快，而第二天夜里院子里的一场火更让那一周变得古怪。"},"utter":{"tw":[["utterly",4],["complete",5],["drop",3],["circulate",2],["shame",6],["dead",0],["raise",3],["communicate",2],["despair",6],["express",0]],"en":"The speaker's first attempt was an utter failure, and he knew it at once. His voice would drop to a whisper, and he could not express a single clear idea. Rumours began to circulate that he had lost his nerve in front of the crowd. It was a complete shame, because his message really mattered to the people there. He said he would rather be dead than raise money for nothing. For a week he was utterly silent and close to despair. Then he learned to communicate with his hands and his eyes instead. In the end the hall understood him better than any written speech.","zh":"那位发言人的第一次尝试彻底失败了，他自己马上就明白。他的声音低成了耳语，一句清楚的意思都表达不出来。于是有人开始传，说他在人群面前没了胆量。这实在可惜，因为他要讲的事对在场的人真有用。他说，与其白张罗一场，还不如死了算了。整整一个星期他一句话也不说，几乎绝望。后来他改用双手和眼睛跟人交流。到最后，全场的人比读任何讲稿都更懂他。"},"vibrate":{"tw":[["vibrant",4],["thrill",0],["hunt",3],["move",2],["modulate",6],["hover",0],["purr",3],["sound",2],["chime",6],["oscillate",0]],"en":"The old sound engineer would vibrate a metal plate to test the speakers in the hall. A pure note would make the plate oscillate, and the needle on the screen would move with it. He could modulate the tone until a small chime rang out through the empty room. Outside the window a bee would hover over the flowers, and its low purr seemed to be part of the music. For him every good concert was a thrill that lasted for days. He would hunt for a dull wire for hours and then fix it in a minute. The whole hall felt more vibrant when he was there.","zh":"那位老音响师会让一块金属板振动起来，以此测试厅里的音箱。一个纯音会让板子来回摆动，屏幕上的指针也跟着走。他能把音调一点点调到位，直到一声轻轻的铃音穿过空荡的屋子。窗外的蜜蜂在花上盘旋，那低低的嗡嗡声仿佛也是音乐的一部分。对他而言，每一场好音乐会都是一种能持续好几天的兴奋。他会为一个发闷的线路找上几个钟头，然后一分钟就修好。有他在的时候，整个大厅都显得更有生气。"},"skip":{"tw":[["skipper",4],["cut",0],["failure",3],["leave",2],["wait",6],["jump",2],["miss",2],["skate",6],["hop",0]],"en":"The skipper of the small ferry told us not to skip the safety talk at the start. He would cut the engine and wait for every passenger to sit down. A young man tried to jump onto the deck too early, and the boat gave a heavy hop in the water. It was a small failure of manners, and the skipper did not miss it. We had to leave the pier late, and one girl chose to skate along the wet planks. Nobody on board wanted to wait any longer. In the end the crossing was quick, and the water stayed calm.","zh":"小渡船的船老大叫我们开头那段安全说明别跳过。他会把发动机熄了，等每位乘客都坐好。一个年轻人抢着往甲板上跳，船在水里猛地颠了一下。这是个小失礼，船老大并没放过。我们只好晚点离岸，还有个女孩干脆在湿木板上溜来溜去。船上没人想再等了。结果这一趟过得很顺，水面一直很平。"},"unify":{"tw":[["unit",4],["mix",0],["pair",3],["integrate",2],["consolidate",6],["unite",0],["bond",3],["entrench",6],["merge",0]],"en":"Two small sports clubs in our town decided to unify into a single unit. Each had its own rules, and it took months to mix the two sets of habits. Older members hoped the pair of teams would merge before the new season began. To integrate the groups, the leaders held a long talk in the old hall. They also wanted to consolidate the money and the fields in one place. A shared bond grew between players who had once been rivals. Some habits were already entrenched in the town, and change came slowly. In the spring the teams did unite under one name.","zh":"我们镇上的两个小体育俱乐部决定合为一体。各有各的规矩，把两套习惯掺到一起花了几个月。老会员希望这对队伍能在新赛季开始前并成一个。为了让两个圈子融到一起，负责人在老礼堂里谈了很久。他们还想把经费和场地都归到一处。原本是对手的球员之间，慢慢结起了一层情谊。有些老习惯在镇上早就扎了根，改变来得很慢。到了春天，两支队伍真的合成了一支。"},"shrink":{"tw":[["contract",3],["blast",3],["move",2],["stretch",1],["surplus",6],["reduce",3],["reef",3],["decrease",2],["grow",6],["wince",0]],"en":"When the new road opened, the small shop began to shrink year by year. The owner had to contract his stock and reduce the number of workers. Sales would decrease in winter and grow again in summer, but the surplus never came back. He would move to a smaller room behind the market and wince at every bill. A blast of cold wind came through the old door all day long. Some weeks the money was so thin that he could not stretch it to Friday. Even the fishing boats near the reef carried fewer visitors.","zh":"新路一通，那家小店就一年比一年萎缩。店主只好收缩存货，裁掉几个工人。冬天卖得少、夏天又好些，可那点盈余再也没回来。他搬到了市场后面一间更小的屋，每看到一张账单都直咧嘴。整天有一股冷风从旧门缝里灌进来。有些星期钱太紧，他连撑到周五都难。连礁石边那些渔船，载来的客人也少了。"},"steep":{"tw":[["plunge",0],["draw",3],["concentrate",2],["gradual",1],["slope",6],["immerse",0],["marinade",3],["soak",2],["climb",6],["infuse",3]],"en":"On the steep slope above the village, the tea pickers would climb before sunrise. The path was so steep that one wrong step could mean a plunge into the rocks below. Down in the kitchen the old cook would immerse the leaves in hot water and let them soak. She liked to marinade the meat first and then infuse the sauce with fresh herbs. Her rules were gradual: draw out the flavour slowly and never concentrate the fire. Sitting by that window, she said, made the hard work of the hill easier. It was a view worth every step.","zh":"村子上方那道陡坡上，采茶人天亮前就得往上爬。路陡得一步踩空就可能翻落到下面的石头上。山下厨房里，老厨娘把茶叶浸在热水里泡开。她喜欢先把肉腌一腌，再用新摘的香草把酱汁㸆出味来。她的做法讲究循序渐进：慢慢把味道熬出来，火候绝不集中在一点上。她说，坐在那扇窗边，山上的辛苦就轻了些。这道风景，值得一步一步爬上去。"},"surrender":{"tw":[["fall",0],["sell",3],["yield",2],["resist",1],["withdraw",6],["deliver",0],["concede",3],["despair",2],["disarm",6],["cede",0]],"en":"After a long strike, the owners decided to surrender and accept the workers' terms. At first the manager tried to resist every demand and refused to yield on pay. The union would not withdraw its plan, and neither side wanted to despair. In the last meeting the company promised to deliver a new contract within a week. The manager had to concede that the old rules were unfair, and he tried to disarm the room with a joke. He would cede control of the schedule to the workers' committee. A small flag was sold at the gate to mark the day. It was a quiet fall of pride, not a defeat.","zh":"僵持了很久之后，厂主们决定让步，答应工人们提出的条件。起初经理还想顶住每一条要求，在工钱上一步不让。工会不肯撤回自己的方案，两边谁也不想就此绝望。最后一次会谈上，公司答应一周内交出新的合同。经理不得不承认旧规矩确实不公，还试着开句玩笑让大家松弛下来。他愿意把排班的事交给工人委员会。门口卖了一面小旗，算是纪念这一天。这是一次平静的收敛，而不是失败。"},"wax":{"tw":[["climb",0],["jump",3],["cover",2],["wane",1],["lacquer",6],["full",0],["advance",3],["increase",2],["ink",6],["rise",0]],"en":"On the night of the full moon the tide would rise and cover the flat rocks near the shore. As the moon would climb over the roof, its light seemed to increase and advance across the wall. My grandmother kept a candle burning, and soft wax would gather in the saucer by midnight. She liked to lacquer small boxes with a brush of dark ink. In the cold months her work would wane, and the shelf stayed empty for weeks. Sometimes the price of her boxes would jump at the market. She wrote every sale in a notebook with the same old pen.","zh":"月圆的那几个晚上，潮水会涨上来，淹没岸边那些平坦的礁石。月亮从屋顶上爬过时，它的光仿佛一点点变强，慢慢铺满整面墙。我奶奶守着一支蜡烛，到半夜蜡油就在碟子里积起一层。她喜欢用深色的墨，把一只只小盒子刷上漆。天冷的月份，她的活计就少了，架子上能空上好几个星期。集市上她那些盒子的价钱有时也会猛地跳一下。她用一个旧本子把每一笔都记下来，笔还是那支。"},"sensation":{"tw":[["sensory",4],["sense",4],["smell",3],["stir",2],["rhythm",6],["genius",0],["taste",3],["faculty",2]],"en":"The first sensation in the hall was a strange quiet before the music began. A good player has a fine sense of rhythm, my teacher always said. She would stir the strings with a slow hand and let the sound rise to the roof. The smell of old wood and dust filled the whole room at once. For her, taste in music was a kind of genius that no test could measure. Each concert trained a different faculty of the ear. What we felt that night was more than a sensory event.","zh":"音乐响起之前，大厅里最先给人的感觉是一阵古怪的安静。老师总说，好的乐手对节奏有极准的分寸。她会用一只手慢慢拨动琴弦，让声音升到房梁。旧木头和灰尘的气味填满了屋子。在她看来，对音乐的品味是一种任何考试都量不出来的天赋。每一场演出都在练耳朵的另一项本事。那一晚我们感到的东西，远不止是感官上的一点反应。"},"repay":{"tw":[["return",0],["restore",3],["answer",2],["disburse",6],["reward",0],["reimburse",3],["pay",2],["compensate",6],["refund",0]],"en":"When a small shop sent the wrong order, the owner promised to repay the customer in full. He would answer every message in person and return the faulty goods without a fuss. The clerk had to disburse a small refund the same day and reimburse the shipping cost. To restore the customer's trust, he added a free gift as a reward for her patience. In the end he had to pay a little more than expected, but the goodwill was worth it. 'We cannot always compensate for lost time,' he said, 'but we can be fair.' The next week the same woman came back and brought a friend.","zh":"一家小店发错了货，老板答应全额赔偿那位顾客。他亲自回复每一条消息，二话不说把有问题的货收回来。店员当天就得支付一笔小额退款，还要补偿运费。为了挽回顾客的信任，他加送了件小礼品，作为她耐心的回报。最后他多花了一点钱，可这份好感很值。他说：'失去的时间我们没法全都补偿，但我们可以公道。'第二个星期，那位女士又回来了，还带来一个朋友。"},"sack":{"tw":[["clear",0],["retire",3],["bag",2],["sacks",6],["fire",0],["dismiss",3],["bed",2],["toss",6],["pocket",0]],"en":"One rainy Monday the manager called the old worker in and told him the company would dismiss him at the end of the month. He had to clear his locker and put his tools into a heavy sack. A thin bag of papers went home with him, and he would toss a few small sacks of spare parts onto the cart. Nobody wanted to fire a man who had worked there for nearly twenty years, yet the firm had no choice. The little money in his pocket felt light, and he worried how he would retire on so little. That night he went straight to bed and slept badly. In the morning he decided to look for work at a smaller yard.","zh":"一个下雨的星期一，经理把这位老工人叫进来，说公司月底就要辞退他。他得清空自己的柜子，把工具装进一条沉甸甸的麻袋。一小袋文件让他带回了家，他还得把几小袋零件扔到推车上。没人愿意开除一个在这儿干了将近二十年的人，可公司别无选择。口袋里那点钱轻飘飘的，他发愁靠这么点怎么退休。那晚他径直上床，却睡得很糟。第二天早上，他决定去一家更小的场地找活干。"},"scramble":{"tw":[["beat",0],["tumble",3],["change",2],["steer",6],["skin",0],["whisk",3],["climb",2],["pull",6],["struggle",2]],"en":"We had to scramble up the rocky hill before the rain came in. My brother would climb first and pull me over the wet stones. Twice I lost my footing and watched a small stone tumble down the slope. A sharp edge took a bit of skin from my knee, and my heart began to beat fast. The wind could whisk my hat away, so I held it tight. We had to steer around a deep gap and change our plan to a safer path. It was a real struggle, but the view from the top made every step worth it.","zh":"我们得赶在下雨前手脚并用地爬上那座石头山。哥哥先爬上去，把我拽过湿滑的石块。我有两次脚下一滑，看着一块小石头滚下坡去。一个尖角从我的膝盖上蹭掉了一小块皮，心跳也快了起来。风会把帽子刮跑，所以我把帽子拽得紧紧的。我们只好绕开一道深沟，把计划改到更安全的小路上。这确实是一场硬撑，但山顶的景色让每一步都值了。"},"scrap":{"tw":[["bit",0],["scale",3],["piece",2],["freeze",6],["chip",0],["shock",3],["waste",2],["import",6],["fight",0]],"en":"At the metal yard, workers sort every scrap into a pile by size and scale. A heavy machine will chip the old cars and cut them into a small piece or a thin bit. In winter the metal can freeze, and the men wear thick gloves all day. The yard imports much of its iron, so a price shock far away can hurt the local trade. Managers hate to waste good steel, and they often fight to keep each order. One cold morning a truck brought a load of broken parts from an old factory. By noon the pile had grown, and the work went on.","zh":"在废金属场里，工人们按大小和规模把每一块废料分堆。一台沉重的机器会把旧车打碎，切成小块或薄片。冬天金属会冻住，工人们整天戴着厚手套。这个场地的大部分铁都靠进口，所以远方一次价格冲击就能伤到本地生意。管理者最恨浪费好钢，常为一笔订单争来争去。一个寒冷的早上，一辆卡车运来一车从旧工厂拆下的破零件。到中午，废料堆高了不少，活还在继续。"},"scrape":{"tw":[["mark",0],["graze",3],["noise",2],["spoon",6],["skin",0],["claw",3],["bow",2],["discard",6],["scratch",0]],"en":"My sister showed me how to scrape the last of the batter from the bowl with a spoon. She would bow her head over the mixture and work the edge with a slow scratch. The thin noise of metal on glass filled the quiet kitchen. Once the spoon slipped and left a small mark on the counter. Our cat stood nearby, ready to graze on anything that fell, its claw tapping the floor. We had to discard the burnt top, because the skin of the cake had turned too dark. By evening the cake was ready, and not a single piece was left.","zh":"姐姐教我怎么用勺子把碗底最后一点面糊刮干净。她低着头，对着那团面糊，慢慢地刮着边。金属刮擦玻璃的轻响充满了安静的厨房。有一次勺子一滑，在台面上留下一道小痕。我们的猫蹲在旁边，随时准备啃食掉下来的东西，爪子还在地板上轻敲。烤焦的那层只好扔掉，因为蛋糕的表皮已经太黑了。到傍晚，蛋糕做好了，一块都没剩下。"},"shaft":{"tw":[["dig",0],["well",3],["beat",2],["pipe",6],["cheat",0],["axle",3],["light",2],["pedal",6],["screw",0]],"en":"The old water pump broke, so my father had to dig around the shaft and reach the well below. Its metal axle was worn, and one thin pipe had a slow leak. He would beat the bent part with a heavy tool and turn each screw by hand. A small light hung on a hook so we could see the wet ground. My job was to pedal the bike that ran the spare pump when the motor failed. Father warned me not to cheat on the count of the turns. By dusk the shaft turned freely again, and cold water came up.","zh":"那台老水泵坏了，父亲只好在竖井四周挖开，够到下面的井。它的金属轴磨坏了，还有一根细管子慢慢漏水。他会用一件重工具敲打弯掉的地方，再用手把每颗螺丝拧上。一盏小灯挂在钩子上，好让我们看清湿漉漉的地面。电机坏的时候，我得蹬那辆带动备用水泵的自行车。父亲提醒我别在转数上作假。到黄昏，轴又转得顺畅了，冰凉的水涌了上来。"},"slap":{"tw":[["bang",0],["cuff",3],["blow",2],["stick",6],["bolt",0],["spank",3],["strike",2],["throw",6],["smack",0]],"en":"That night a wild storm began to slap the thin roof above our room. A loose shutter would bang against the wall, and a long branch began to smack the glass. My uncle had to strike a match and check the back door twice. He pulled his cuff over his hand and took a stick to push the window shut. Then a bright bolt of lightning lit the sky, followed by a heavy blow of thunder. When my little cousin joked about the noise, uncle gave him a playful spank. He would throw a dry cloth over the wet floor and laugh, telling us the worst had passed.","zh":"那天夜里，一场狂风暴雨开始抽打我们头顶那层薄屋顶。一扇松动的百叶窗拍着墙，一根长树枝也开始敲打玻璃。叔叔只好划亮一根火柴，把后门检查了两遍。他把袖口拉下来罩住手，拿起一根棍子去把窗推上。接着一道亮闪划过天空，随后是一记沉闷的雷声。小表弟拿这响动开玩笑时，叔叔轻轻拍了他一下。他又扔了块干布盖在湿地板上，笑着告诉我们最坏的一阵已经过去了。"},"snatch":{"tw":[["bit",0],["mesh",3],["touch",2],["jerk",6],["catch",0],["rebound",3],["capture",2],["knock",6],["grab",0]],"en":"In the last minute of the game, our best player tried to snatch the ball from the tall boy on the other team. He had to grab it with both hands and keep a light touch on the ground. A quick jerk of his wrist sent the ball through the white mesh of the net. The other side would catch the rebound and knock two players aside to score. My friend said we had only one more chance to capture the lead. A small bit of luck and a fast move would decide the day. When the whistle blew, our team had won by a single point.","zh":"比赛最后一分钟，我们最好的球员想从对方那个高个子手里抢下球。他得用双手抓住球，同时还要轻轻点着地面。他手腕猛地一抖，球穿过白色网兜进了筐。对方抢下篮板，撞开我们两名球员得分。朋友说我们只剩一次机会反超比分。一点运气加上快速移动，就能决定这一天。哨响时，我们队以一分之差赢了。"},"soak":{"tw":[["hook",0],["brew",3],["beat",2],["boil",6],["drink",2],["steep",3],["drain",6],["plume",0],["pluck",0]],"en":"On a slow Sunday my grandmother taught me how to soak dried leaves in hot water. She would pluck a few fresh leaves from the small tree and hang them on a hook to dry. Then she had to boil the water and let the leaves steep for five minutes. A thin plume of steam rose from the pot and filled the kitchen. She liked to brew a mild drink for the whole family, and she would beat one egg for a small cake. Afterward we had to drain the used leaves and throw them into the garden. That warm cup stayed with me all afternoon.","zh":"一个悠闲的星期天，奶奶教我把干叶子泡在热水里。她会从那棵小树上摘下几片鲜叶，挂在钩子上晾干。然后她要把水烧开，让叶子闷上五分钟。一缕细细的蒸汽从壶里升起，充满了厨房。她喜欢给全家泡一壶温和的饮料，还会打一个鸡蛋做小蛋糕。之后我们得把用过的叶子滤掉，扔进园子里。那杯热茶陪了我一下午。"},"sphere":{"tw":[["field",0],["ball",3],["surface",2],["dimension",6],["sector",0],["drop",3],["aspect",2],["integral",6],["domain",0]],"en":"In the geography class the teacher set a small globe on the table, a painted ball that showed the whole sphere at once. She asked us to run a finger over its smooth surface and find our own field. 'Every drop of water,' she said, 'belongs to one great domain of the earth.' We learned that each orbit of a moon adds a new dimension to what we know. The ice near the poles is an integral part of the whole picture. Farming is only one sector of the economy, and a dry aspect of the land can change it. By the end, the class saw the world as one round whole.","zh":"地理课上，老师把一个小地球仪放在桌上，那是一个彩绘的球，一眼就能看出整个球体。她让我们用手指滑过它光滑的表面，找出自己所在的那片领域。她说：'每一滴水，都属于地球一个辽阔的领域。'我们学到，月球每绕行一圈，都会为我们已知的东西添上一个新的维度。两极附近的冰，是整幅图景中不可分割的一部分。农业只是经济中的一个部门，而土地干燥的一面会改变它。下课时，全班都把这世界看成了一个浑圆的整体。"},"spike":{"tw":[["ear",0],["pin",3],["change",2],["surge",6],["lace",0],["spear",3],["rise",2],["trigger",6],["fortify",0]],"en":"At the market stall the cook was busy with a new dish when a sudden change in the weather brought a spike in customers. An ear of corn and a few green spears of asparagus lay beside a pin on her apron. She had to lace the roast with thin string and fortify the soup with fresh spice. The heat would trigger a quick surge in steam, so she kept the lid loose on the pot. Demand began to rise, and by noon the queue reached the far corner. She smiled and said the season always brings such small surprises.","zh":"集市摊位上，厨子正忙着做一道新菜，天气忽然一变，又带来一阵客流高峰。一个玉米棒和几根嫩绿的芦笋放在她围裙上的别针旁。她得用细绳把烤肉缠好，再用新鲜的香料给汤提味。火一热就会腾起一股蒸汽，所以她把锅盖留得松松的。需求开始上涨，到中午队伍已经排到了远处的拐角。她笑着说，这个季节总会带来这样的小惊喜。"},"splash":{"tw":[["stir",0],["salt",3],["dirty",2],["hot",6],["sprinkle",0],["drizzle",3],["noise",2],["slick",6],["slop",0]],"en":"My mother let me stir the warm soup while she cut the fresh bread. I added a pinch of salt and a light sprinkle of herbs on top. A small drizzle of oil made the surface look slick and bright. When I moved too fast, a hot drop gave a loud splash and marked my shirt. 'Be careful,' she said, 'or soup will slop onto the dirty floor.' The soft noise of the boiling pot filled the room, and I slowed my hand. That evening the soup tasted better than it ever had before.","zh":"妈妈让我搅汤，她自己去切面包。我撒了一小撮盐，又在上面轻轻洒了点香草。几滴油落下去，汤面变得油亮亮、滑溜溜的。我动作一快，一滴热汤溅起来，在我衬衫上留下印子。她说：'当心点，不然汤会洒到脏地板上。'锅里翻滚的轻响充满了厨房，我放慢了手。那天晚上，这锅汤比以往任何时候都好喝。"},"stab":{"tw":[["dig",0],["lunge",3],["blow",2],["wound",6],["knife",0],["bayonet",3],["attempt",2],["puncture",6],["poke",0]],"en":"At the old battlefield dig, a student bent down to poke the soil with a small tool. She had to dig slowly, because one hard blow could break a fragile blade. In the tray lay a rusted knife and the thin bayonet of an old rifle. The guide explained how such a point could puncture cloth and leave a deep stab wound. He added that not every wound on old bones came from a real fight. On her second lunge at the clay, she found a small metal ring. The whole attempt took three weeks, but it gave the museum a real story.","zh":"在旧战场的发掘现场，一个学生弯下腰，用小工具戳着泥土。她得慢慢挖，因为一下重击就可能弄坏脆弱的刀片。托盘里放着一把锈刀和一支旧步枪上细细的刺刀。讲解员说明这样的尖头如何刺穿布料，留下一道深深的刺伤。他还说，并非老骨头上的每一道伤都来自真正的搏斗。她第二次猛地扎向黏土时，找到了一枚小小的金属环。整个尝试花了三周，却给博物馆留下了一个真实的故事。"},"stack":{"tw":[["deal",0],["flood",3],["arrange",2],["log",6],["lot",0],["funnel",3],["list",2],["frame",6],["mess",0]],"en":"On my first day at the office, a tall stack of papers covered the whole desk. My manager said a great deal of mail had come in after a flood of new orders. I had to arrange each sheet and write a short log of every call. There was a long list of names, and a lot of them were hard to read. A plastic funnel sat in a corner, left over from some old job. The frame of the notice board was broken, and the whole room was a mess. By evening the stack had shrunk, and I could finally breathe.","zh":"上班第一天，一摞高高的文件铺满了整张桌子。经理说，新订单一涌而来之后，来了一大堆邮件。我只好把每张纸分好类，把每个电话都记成一小段日志。名单拉得很长，其中很多名字都难认。角落里放着一个塑料漏斗，不知是哪个旧活留下的。公告栏的边框坏了，整个房间乱糟糟的。到傍晚，那摞文件矮了不少，我才终于能喘口气。"},"startle":{"tw":[["jump",0],["shy",3],["move",2],["bewilder",6],["start",0],["wince",3],["shock",2],["annoy",6],["galvanize",0]],"en":"The sudden ring of a phone seemed to startle everyone in the quiet reading room. I gave a small jump and saw a shy girl near the shelf wince. Nobody dared to move for a moment, and the noise began to annoy an older reader. It was a real shock, because the room had been silent from the start. Such a loud sound can bewilder anyone who is deep in a book. Then the clerk hurried over to turn it off, which seemed to galvanize the whole staff. In a minute the room was calm again, and we all went back to our pages.","zh":"一阵突兀的电话铃，似乎把安静阅览室里的人都吓了一跳。我微微一跳，看见书架旁一个害羞的女孩皱起了脸。有一刻谁也不敢动，那响声还开始惹恼了一位年长的读者。这真是让人吃惊，因为屋里从一开头就静得很。这么大的声音，会让埋头读书的人一下子发懵。随后店员赶紧跑过去把它关掉，这一下像是把整个员工都鼓动起来了。不到一分钟，屋里又静了下来，我们各自回到书页上。"},"steer":{"tw":[["head",0],["corner",3],["control",2],["push",6],["lead",0],["park",3],["male",2],["pull",6],["wind",0]],"en":"On his first driving lesson, my brother had to steer the small car through the narrow streets. He kept his head calm and held the wheel with both hands. At one sharp corner he had to control the speed and gently push the pedal. A tall male driver behind us began to pull close, which made him nervous. His teacher told him to lead with his eyes and look far ahead. They had to park in a tight space near the old mill, where the road began to wind. Step by step, he learned to steer without fear.","zh":"第一次上路学车时，弟弟得开着小车穿过狭窄的街道。他稳住心神，双手握着方向盘。在一个急弯处，他要控制住车速，轻轻踩下踏板。后面一位高个子男司机开始贴得很近，弄得他有点紧张。教练让他眼睛往前带，看得远一点。他们还得把车停进老磨坊旁一个很窄的位置，那里的路开始拐弯。一步一步，他学会了不再害怕地驾驶。"},"sting":{"tw":[["burn",0],["prickle",3],["force",2],["throat",6],["stick",0],["nettle",3],["hurt",2],["poison",6],["bite",0]],"en":"On a summer walk my sister brushed against a nettle and felt its sting at once. The small hairs would stick to her skin and leave a sharp prickle. It did not hurt for long, but the spot began to burn like a light fever. She had to force herself not to scratch it with her nails. A cool drink eased her dry throat, and she soon stopped complaining. Later she learned that the poison in such plants is weak for most people. A bee bite would have been far worse, she said with a smile.","zh":"一个夏天的散步中，妹妹蹭到了一株荨麻，立刻感到了那种刺痛。细小的绒毛会粘在她皮肤上，留下一阵尖锐的刺痒。疼得不久，但那块地方开始火烧火燎，像有点低烧。她只好硬忍着，不让指甲去挠。一杯凉饮润了润她发干的喉咙，她很快就不再抱怨了。后来她才知道，这类植物里的毒素对大多数人来说很轻微。她笑着说，要是被蜜蜂咬一口，那可就糟多了。"},"strand":{"tw":[["ground",0],["barb",3],["form",2],["loop",6],["chain",0],["ply",3],["land",2],["roundabout",6],["string",0]],"en":"My grandfather showed me how to mend the wire fence that ran across his land. Each strand had to be pulled tight and joined into a small loop. A sharp barb had cut his glove, so he wrapped a cloth around his hand. He would lay the wire on the ground and count every ply before he cut it. A long chain of posts stood along the field, and a roundabout path led to the far gate. He tied one end with a string so the wire would not slip. By noon the fence took its old form again.","zh":"爷爷教我怎么修补横穿他地里的铁丝围栏。每一股都得拉紧，再拧成一个小环。一个尖尖的倒刺划破了他的手套，他便用布把手裹上。他总是把铁丝放在地上，数清每一股再下剪。田边立着长长一链木桩，一条绕远的路径通往远处的门。他用绳子把一头系住，免得铁丝滑开。到中午，围栏又恢复了原来的样子。"},"strap":{"tw":[["whip",2],["cat",3],["beat",2],["toe",6],["lash",0],["switch",3],["tie",2],["rope",6],["slash",0]],"en":"The night we sailed across the bay, the wind began to beat the small boat. My job was to lash the sail and tie every loose rope with a strong strap. A wave threw me off balance and I banged my toe on the rail. Our old cat hid under the seat while a cold rain began to slash the deck. The captain had to whip the wet rope around the mast before it could slip. He found a wooden switch to hold the torn cover down. By dawn the storm passed, and the bay lay still.","zh":"我们横渡海湾的那晚，风开始拍打这条小船。我的活是用结实的皮带把帆绑紧，把每一根松绳都系好。一个浪把我晃得失了平衡，脚趾撞到了栏杆上。我们那只老猫躲在座位下，冷冷的雨开始横扫甲板。船长赶紧把湿绳子在桅杆上缠紧，免得它滑开。他找了根木棍把破了的帆布压住。天亮时风暴过去了，海湾一片平静。"},"subordinate":{"tw":[["subsidiary",0],["man",3],["rate",2],["dominant",1],["rank",6],["subdue",0],["associate",5],["word",2],["intermediary",6]],"en":"A young man joined a large firm as a subordinate in the sales team. His rank was low, and at first he had to subdue his wish to argue. The dominant voice in every meeting belonged to the head of the department. A small subsidiary office handled the slower work and reported through an intermediary. He would associate with clerks and managers at the same rate, no matter their title. In one short word, the boss told him to be patient. Over a year he learned that a quiet worker is often the most useful one.","zh":"一个年轻人进了家大公司，在销售组里当了个属下。他职级不高，起初只好压住自己想争辩的念头。每次会上说了算的，都是部门主管的声音。一个小附属办事处负责较慢的活，通过一个中间人来汇报。他对文员和经理一视同仁，不论对方头衔如何。老板用简短的一个字让他耐心些。一年下来他明白了，安静的员工往往最有用。"},"tag":{"tw":[["dog",0],["tree",3],["touch",2],["card",6],["mark",0],["brand",3],["attach",2],["ring",6],["tail",0]],"en":"A small dog followed me home and sat beside the old tree in our yard. I looked for a tag on its neck and found a metal ring with a name. The brand on the little card was one I did not know. I had to attach a note to its collar and call the number twice. It wanted to touch my hand with its nose and would not stop wagging its tail. The mark on its ear seemed old and faded. By evening its owner arrived, and the dog ran off with a happy bark.","zh":"一只小狗跟着我回了家，蹲在我们院子那棵老树边。我找它脖子上的牌子，发现一个刻着名字的金属环。那张小卡片上的牌子我认不出来。我只好在它项圈上系了张纸条，又照号码打了两遍。它想用鼻子碰我的手，尾巴摇个不停。它耳朵上的那道印子看着又旧又淡。傍晚，它的主人来了，狗高兴地叫了一声跑开了。"},"thread":{"tw":[["draw",0],["cotton",3],["arrange",2],["rope",6],["wind",0],["pile",3],["travel",2],["yarn",6],["string",0]],"en":"My grandmother taught me how to thread a needle on a rainy afternoon. She would draw a long piece of cotton from the spool and wind it around her finger. Then she had to arrange the cloth on her knees and find the torn seam. A thick rope of yarn lay in a pile beside her old basket. She said the same thin string could travel through many layers and hold them together. I watched her steady hands and tried to copy every small move. By evening the coat looked almost new.","zh":"一个下雨的午后，奶奶教我怎么穿针引线。她会从线轴上抽出一长段棉线，在手指上绕一圈。接着她得把布料摊在膝上，找到裂开的那道缝。一团粗毛线堆在她旧篮子旁边。她说，同样一根细线能穿过许多层布，把它们连在一起。我看着她稳稳的手，努力照着每个小动作去做。到傍晚，那件外套看上去几乎跟新的一样。"},"thrust":{"tw":[["drive",0],["dig",3],["blow",2],["tilt",6],["force",0],["pop",3],["move",2],["muzzle",6],["push",2]],"en":"In the workshop my uncle tried to free a stuck part with one hard thrust. He had to drive a thin tool into the gap and dig out the old rust. Each blow of the hammer sent a small puff of dust into the air. The heavy frame began to tilt, so he used more force to hold it steady. A cap would pop off and move across the floor. His old dog watched from the corner, its muzzle resting on its paws. In the end a firm push finished the job.","zh":"在车间里，叔叔猛力一推，想把卡住的零件弄松。他得把一件细工具敲进缝里，把旧锈挖出来。锤子每落一下，就有一小股灰尘腾起来。沉重的框架开始倾斜，他只好用更大的力气把它扶稳。一个盖子啪地弹开，从地板上滑了过去。他的老狗从角落里看着，口鼻搁在爪子上。最后，使劲一推，活干完了。"},"tilt":{"tw":[["list",3],["fight",3],["move",2],["throttle",6],["rock",0],["weather",3],["position",2],["thrust",6],["lean",0]],"en":"That morning the small boat began to tilt as the wind grew strong. I had to list everything we owned and tie it down before each wave. The captain would fight the wheel and move the throttle with a slow hand. Every rock of the hull made my bag slide across the floor. The cold weather did not help, and the rain never stopped. He asked me to keep my position near the mast and lean with the boat. One last thrust from a big wave nearly threw us over, but we held on.","zh":"那天早上，风一大，小船就开始倾斜。我只好把所有家当列出来，在每个浪来之前把它们绑牢。船长一边和舵较劲，一边慢慢推动油门。船身每一次摇晃，都让我的包滑过地板。寒冷的天气帮不上忙，雨也一直没停。他让我守在桅杆旁的位置上，跟着船一起侧身。最后一个大浪猛地一顶，差点把我们掀翻，可我们撑住了。"},"timber":{"tw":[["forest",0],["board",3],["land",2],["mill",6],["quality",0],["register",3],["post",2],["coal",6],["tone",0]],"en":"The old mill stood at the edge of a wide forest, where workers cut timber all year. Every board had to pass a check for quality before it left the yard. A tall post near the gate marked the land that belonged to the family. The mill kept a register of each load and burned coal to heat the drying room. My uncle would run a finger along the wood and speak in a warm tone. He said good timber lasts longer than any cheap board. That winter the forest gave them work when little else did.","zh":"老木材厂坐落在宽阔森林的边缘，工人们一年到头都在那里伐木。每一块木板出厂前都得过一道质量检查。大门边立着一根高高的柱子，标出属于这户人家的地。厂里把每一批货都登记在册，还烧煤给烘干房加热。叔叔会用手指顺着木头摸过去，用温暖的语气说话。他说好木料比任何便宜板子都耐用。那年冬天，别的活少，森林却给了他们生计。"},"torture":{"tw":[["agony",0],["boot",3],["pain",2],["subjected",6],["rack",3],["martyr",3],["injure",2],["abuse",6],["anguish",0]],"en":"The climber was injured high on the ridge, and his family waited in real anguish. For hours his leg gave him such agony that he could hardly speak. The doctor said the damage was not serious, but he was subjected to a long and painful night. His mother called him a martyr for hiding his pain so well. He was placed on a rack of thin boards to keep the leg straight, and a nurse changed his heavy boot for a soft shoe. He hated the abuse his body had taken, yet he refused to give up. By morning the torture of that night had passed, and he smiled.","zh":"那名登山者在山脊高处受了伤，家人焦急万分地等着。有好几个小时，他的腿疼得钻心，几乎说不出话。医生说伤得不重，可他还是熬过了一个漫长而痛苦的夜晚。母亲说他忍着疼不吭声，像个小受难者。他被架上几块薄板，好让腿保持伸直，护士把他沉重的登山靴换成了一双软鞋。他恨自己身体受的这些罪，却不肯放弃。到早上，那一夜的折磨过去了，他笑了。"},"tumble":{"tw":[["fall",0],["roll",3],["drop",2],["plunge",6],["tip",0],["somersault",3],["move",2],["slide",6],["collapse",0]],"en":"On a bright Saturday the children ran to the grassy hill and let themselves tumble down. Each fall ended in a loud laugh, and then they would roll back up again. One boy tried a quick somersault and nearly lost his shoes. A sudden drop in the path and a place where it began to tip made another child slide into a soft bush. The little ones would move slowly at first, then take a brave plunge to the bottom. No one wanted the game to collapse in tears, so they took turns. By evening every coat was green with grass.","zh":"一个晴朗的星期六，孩子们跑到草坡上，任由自己滚下来。每一次摔倒都伴着一声大笑，然后他们又摇摇晃晃地爬回去。有个男孩想翻个跟头，差点把鞋甩掉。小路在一处开始打斜，另一个孩子便滑进了软软的灌木丛里。小一点的先慢慢挪动，然后壮着胆子往坡底一冲。谁也不想让游戏哭哭啼啼地收场，于是大家轮流来。到傍晚，每件外套都染上了草绿色。"},"warrant":{"tw":[["guarantee",0],["cover",3],["back",2],["arrest",6],["justify",0],["pardon",3],["confirm",2],["custody",6],["sanction",0]],"en":"The officer said the new evidence did not warrant such a serious charge. He could not arrest the young man without a proper reason, and the old papers would only confirm the date. The law could not guarantee a fair result unless both sides had time to speak. A witness would back the story and cover every detail of that night. The judge asked whether the police had a warrant to search the back room. In the end she chose to pardon the small mistake and released him from custody. 'No rule can justify a wrong,' she said, 'and I will not sanction one.'","zh":"警官说，新证据不足以让这么严重的指控成立。没有正当理由，他不能逮捕那个年轻人，而旧文件只能确认日期。除非双方都有时间说话，法律无法保证公正的结果。一名证人会支持这个说法，把那天晚上的一切细节都讲清楚。法官问警方是否有搜查后屋的搜查令。最后她决定对小过失予以宽恕，把他从拘留中放了出来。她说：'没有哪条规矩能为错误开脱，我不会批准这种事。'"},"regress":{"tw":[["return",0],["recover",3],["change",2],["progress",1],["oscillate",6],["lapse",0],["procreate",6],["revert",2]],"en":"When the old dam was removed, the small wetland began to recover year by year. At first the number of birds seemed to progress, then it would regress after a dry summer. The water level would oscillate with the seasons, up and down. If the fence broke, the herd would return to the old fields and the young could not procreate in peace. A single lapse in care could change the whole valley again. Rangers feared the land might revert to a dry, empty place. So they watched the ponds and mended every gap. Now the birds come back each spring, and the marsh is full of sound.","zh":"大坝拆掉后，那片小湿地一年年慢慢复原。起初鸟的数量像是在增加，可一个旱夏过后又会倒退。水位会随季节来回摆动，涨了又落。围栏一破，兽群就会回到旧地，幼崽也没法安静地繁衍。照料上稍有疏忽，就能让整个山谷再次变样。巡护员担心这片地会退回到干燥空旷的样子。于是他们守着池塘，把每处缺口都补上。如今每年春天鸟都回来，沼泽里满是声响。"},"repress":{"tw":[["reduce",0],["swallow",3],["change",2],["coerce",6],["suppress",2],["forget",2],["agitate",6],["muffle",0]],"en":"At the family dinner my brother tried hard to repress his anger about the bill. He would swallow a sharp reply and change the subject to the weather. His hands began to agitate under the table, but he kept his voice low. To suppress a cough, he drank water and looked at the wall. He did not want to coerce anyone into taking his side. When the noise grew, he had to muffle a laugh behind his hand. He tried to reduce the tension with a quiet joke. Nobody knew he had to forget his own pride, and the evening passed peacefully.","zh":"家庭聚餐上，我哥哥拼命压住对那笔账的火气。他会咽下一句刻薄话，把话题转到天气上去。他的手在桌下开始躁动，可声音一直压得很低。为了忍住咳嗽，他喝了口水，眼睛看着墙。他不想逼任何人站到他这边。闹声上来时，他只好用手捂住一声笑。他想用一个不痛不痒的玩笑缓解紧张。谁也不知道他得先把自己的面子放下，那个晚上就平平静静地过去了。"},"retrieve":{"tw":[["find",0],["access",3],["bring",2],["locate",6],["remember",0],["recognize",3],["collect",6],["think",0]],"en":"When our dog ran off in the park, we had to retrieve him before dark. I tried to remember where he liked to run and to think about the paths. My sister went to find the old gate he always slipped through. We could not access the far field, so we had to collect a key from the shed. Then we began to locate his small prints near the stream. At last I could recognize a white shape behind the bushes. I called, and he came at once, wet and happy. We had to bring him home on a lead, tired but safe.","zh":"公园里我们的狗跑丢了，天黑前我们得把它找回来。我努力回想它爱去哪儿跑，想着那些小路。妹妹去找它总钻出去的那道旧门。远处那片地我们进不去，只好去小棚里取一把钥匙。然后我们沿着溪边找起它的小爪印。终于，我认出灌木丛后一个白白的身影。我一喊，它立刻跑了过来，浑身湿透，高兴得很。我们只好牵着它回家，累是累，好歹平安。"},"rib":{"tw":[["guy",0],["tease",3],["bone",2],["elbow",6],["roast",0],["vein",3],["cut",2],["bruise",6]],"en":"During the busy Sunday match a young guy fell hard and hurt his lower rib. The bone was not broken, but a dark bruise spread under his arm. His brother would tease him all evening about the clumsy fall. Once he raised his elbow too fast, and the pain cut through his side. A thin vein on his wrist showed how hard his heart was beating. The family tried to roast him gently while he lay on the sofa. He only laughed and asked for more soup. By Monday morning he could walk again, though still slowly and with care.","zh":"周日的比赛里，一个小伙子重重摔倒，伤到了下面一根肋骨。骨头没断，但腋下泛起一片乌青。他哥哥整晚都拿他摔得笨来打趣。有一回他抬手太快，疼得一下穿过身侧。手腕上一条细血管，看得出他心跳得多厉害。他躺在沙发上时，一家人轻轻逗他。他只顾笑，还嚷着要再喝碗汤。到周一早上他已经能走了，虽然还慢，还小心。"},"roast":{"tw":[["guy",0],["tease",3],["cook",2],["lamb",6],["knock",0],["cut",2],["veal",6],["joint",0]],"en":"On Sunday my father would roast a piece of lamb for the whole family. He liked to cook it slowly and to cut it at the table himself. A young guy from next door came to help and stayed to eat. My sister would tease him about the burnt joint on the plate. He answered with a joke and a loud knock on the table. My mother served a small piece of veal beside the soft potatoes. The smell filled the room and made everyone hungry. We talked for hours, and no one wanted to leave.","zh":"星期天父亲会烤一块羊肉，给全家人吃。他喜欢慢慢烤，还喜欢自己在上桌时动刀切。隔壁一个小伙子过来帮忙，也就留下来吃饭。我妹妹会拿盘子里那块烤过头的肉打趣他。他回敬一句玩笑，还在桌上重重敲了一下。母亲在旁边配了一小块小牛肉和软烂的土豆。香味灌满屋子，把每个人都勾饿了。我们聊了好几个钟头，谁也不想起身走。"},"rotate":{"tw":[["revolve",0],["wheel",3],["grow",2],["fold",6],["splay",0],["screw",3],["serve",2],["clockwise",6]],"en":"Every year the farmers in our valley rotate their crops to keep the soil rich. The old mill wheel would revolve all day, slow and heavy. Wheat would grow in one field while beans filled another. My grandfather liked to serve a simple meal to the workers at noon. To fix the mill, he had to screw a new handle into the frame. Then he showed me how the fan blades fold and splay when they turn. He always turned the small wheel clockwise, never the other way. It was a simple lesson I still remember.","zh":"我们山谷里的农户每年轮换种植，好让土地保持肥沃。那座老磨坊的水轮整天慢慢地转。一块地里长麦子时，另一块就种满豆子。爷爷喜欢中午给工人们做一顿简单的饭。要修磨坊，他得把一个新把手拧进框里。然后他教我看扇叶转动时怎么折起来、又怎么张开。他总是把小轮子朝顺时针方向转，从不反着来。这道理很简单，我一直记着。"},"savage":{"tw":[["wild",5],["cannibal",3],["knock",2],["barbarian",6],["cruel",0],["primitive",2],["menace",6],["wolf",0]],"en":"My grandfather used to tell us about a savage storm he met near a far shore. He said the wind was like a wild beast that would knock the boat on its side. On the island lived a tribe he called cruel and primitive, though he never went ashore. The men there, he said, were like a wolf pack in the dark. He told of a barbarian chief and even a cannibal tale that made us shiver. To him the whole coast was a menace, not a home. Still, he never spoke with hate, only with wonder. We listened until the lamp burned low.","zh":"爷爷以前常给我们讲，他在远方一片海岸遇上的那场凶猛的暴风。他说风像一头野兽，能把船掀翻在一边。岛上住着他称之为残酷、原始的一族，不过他从没上岸。那里的男人，他说，像黑暗中一群狼。他讲到一个蛮族头领，还讲了个吃人的故事，听得我们直发抖。在他眼里，整条海岸都是威胁，不是家园。可他讲这些时从无恨意，只有惊奇。我们一直听到灯油快尽。"},"scent":{"tw":[["nose",0],["incense",3],["groom",2],["glow",6],["smell",2],["musk",3],["purple",6],["wind",0]],"en":"In the little shop on the lane the air held a rich scent of wood and spice. A thin stick of incense burned near the door and left a soft glow of smoke. My aunt would groom each bottle and wipe the glass before opening. She let me smell three oils and pick the one I liked. One had a deep musk, and another was light, like warm wind in summer. A purple label marked the newest bottle on the shelf. My nose could still catch the mix long after we left. That shop always made me walk more slowly.","zh":"巷子里那间小店里，空气里带着一股浓浓的木头和香料的气味。门边点着一根细香，留下一丝淡淡的烟光。我姑妈会一瓶瓶擦拭干净，开门前把玻璃擦亮。她让我闻三种香油，挑我喜欢的那种。一种有很深的麝香，另一种很淡，像夏日里暖洋洋的风。货架上最新的一瓶贴着紫色标签。我们离开很久之后，我的鼻子还能抓住那股混合的香。那家店总让我走得慢一些。"},"sparkle":{"tw":[["light",0],["seethe",3],["flash",2],["shine",6],["spark",0],["emit",2],["exude",6],["foam",0]],"en":"On the night of the town festival the old fountain began to sparkle under the lamps. The water seemed to seethe and send white foam over the stone rim. A small electric light made each drop flash like a tiny star. From the dark sky one bright spark flew down and was gone. The surface would shine for a second, then grow still again. My friend said the water could emit a cool breath on a hot night. Some said the pool would exude a strange calm that drew people in. We sat on the wall until the lights went out.","zh":"镇上办节的那晚，老喷泉在灯下开始闪光。水像是沸腾起来，把白沫溅到石沿外。一盏小灯让每一滴水珠都像一颗小星星那样闪。黑黢黢的天上，一颗亮火星落下来，转眼就不见了。水面会亮一下，然后又静下来。朋友说，水在热天里能散发出一股凉气。有人说这池子会透出一种奇特的安宁，把人吸引过去。我们在矮墙上一直坐到灯灭。"},"spit":{"tw":[["tongue",0],["drool",3],["rain",2],["mouth",6],["sprinkle",0],["pin",2],["snake",6],["saliva",0]],"en":"On a warm afternoon my sister fed her baby on a cloth in the garden. The child would spit out the soft food and let a thin drool run down his chin. He poked his tongue out at us and laughed at his own joke. A light rain began to sprinkle the grass, so we moved under the tree. My sister had to pin the cloth down before it blew away. Beside the fence a long snake slid past with its mouth open, hunting. I could feel the cold air on my own cheek like wet saliva. We packed up and went inside before the storm.","zh":"一个暖和的下午，姐姐在院子里的布上给孩子喂饭。孩子会把软软的食物吐出来，让一缕口水顺着下巴流下来。他冲我们吐出舌头，还为自己的把戏直笑。细细的雨开始洒在草地上，我们就挪到大树底下。姐姐只好把布按住，免得被风吹走。篱笆旁边，一条长蛇张着嘴游过去，在找吃的。我自己的脸颊上能感到一股凉气，像湿湿的唾液。我们在风雨来之前收拾东西进了屋。"},"spy":{"tw":[["sight",0],["tail",3],["monitor",2],["espionage",6],["spot",0],["detect",3],["secret",6],["stag",0]],"en":"Before sunrise a wildlife watcher sat still, hoping to spy on a shy stag by the lake. He kept his sight fixed on the far trees and would monitor every small move. The deer's tail flicked as it stepped into the open, and he began to spot the rest of the herd. To catch a secret moment he used a long lens and held his breath. He did not want to detect any sound from his own body, so he wore soft shoes. In his mind the work felt like quiet espionage in a green world. At last the big stag turned its head toward him. One picture was enough, and he left without a noise.","zh":"日出前，一位看野生动物的人一动不动地坐着，想偷偷看湖边那只胆小的雄鹿。他目光始终盯着远处的树林，盯着每一个小动作。鹿尾一甩，它走了出来，他这才看清余下的鹿群。为了抓到那秘密的一刻，他用了一支长镜头，屏住呼吸。他不想让自己的身体发出一点声响，于是穿了软底鞋。在他心里，这活儿就像在绿色的世界里做一次安静的谍探。终于，那头大雄鹿把头转向了他。一张就够了，他悄没声地离开。"},"streak":{"tw":[["bar",0],["band",3],["move",2],["straight",6],["run",2],["flash",2],["outing",6],["stripe",0]],"en":"On the school outing the children lined up for a short race across the field. Each runner wore a bright band on the arm and a stripe on the shirt. When the teacher called, they began to run straight toward the far bar of shade. One boy put on a sudden flash of speed and took the lead. A thin streak of dust rose behind the last runner. My cousin could not move faster, but he did not stop. The winner was kind and helped him to the finish. It was the finest outing of the whole term.","zh":"学校出游那天，孩子们排好队，在田野上跑一小段。每个选手臂上系一条亮带子，衫上有一道条纹。老师一喊，他们就朝远处那片树荫直直地跑。一个男孩猛地发力，冲到最前面。最后一名身后扬起一道细细的尘线。我表弟快不起来，可他没停下。得胜的孩子心好，还扶他到了终点。那是这一学期最好的一次出游。"},"suppress":{"tw":[["inhibit",0],["silence",3],["control",2],["resist",6],["oppress",0],["swallow",3],["incite",6],["repress",3]],"en":"When the factory planned to close, the workers tried to resist in a calm way. The manager wanted to inhibit the staff and suppress the news until the deal was signed. He tried to silence the union and to control what was said in the yard. The owners, he said, would not oppress anyone, yet they would not talk either. A few loud men began to incite the younger staff to walk out. The older ones chose to swallow their anger and wait. They knew the firm could repress any open protest with a single letter. In the end the plant stayed open, but no one felt safe.","zh":"厂子要关的消息一出，工人们想用平静的方式抗争。经理既想压住员工，也想把这消息压到合同签定为止。他想让工会闭嘴，还想管住院子里说出去的话。他说，老板们不会欺压任何人，可他们也不肯谈。几个大嗓门的人开始鼓动年轻员工罢工走人。年纪大的却选择把火气咽下去，等着。他们清楚，公司一封信就能压下任何公开的抗议。最后厂子还是开着，可谁都没有安全感。"},"tangle":{"tw":[["drag",0],["involve",2],["jumble",6],["sweep",0],["twist",2],["squabble",6],["knot",0]],"en":"On Saturday morning the garden hose lay in a hopeless tangle near the wall. My father had to drag it across the wet grass and twist it back into a straight line. Inside, the kids would squabble over a game and involve the whole house in noise. The wires under the desk were a real jumble, and I had to sweep the dust away first. He showed me how to find the end and to loosen each knot. It took an hour, but at last the water ran free. Then we both sat down with cold drinks. The yard looked calm again, and so did we.","zh":"周六早上，花园的水管在墙边缠成一团乱麻。父亲只好把它拖过湿草地，一点点扭成直的一条。屋里孩子们为一局游戏吵嘴，把整栋房子都卷进吵闹里。桌下的电线真是一团乱，我得先把灰扫开。他教我找到头，再把一个个结松开。这花了我们一个钟头，水总算顺畅地流了出来。然后我们俩坐下来喝凉饮。院子又显得平静了，我们也是。"},"tick":{"tw":[["beat",0],["receipt",3],["sound",2],["bite",6],["check",0],["sew",2],["rabbit",6],["mark",2]],"en":"In the small tailor's shop a tall clock kept a steady tick all day. The owner would sit and sew while its beat filled the quiet room. She liked the sound of it and would check the old machine beside her. On the wall she kept a written mark for every finished order. When a buyer came in, she wrote a receipt and thanked him for the work. Her young rabbit slept in a box near the door. One evening a small insect gave her a bite on the arm. She laughed, put a plaster on, and went back to the clock.","zh":"那家小裁缝店里，一座高钟整天滴答个不停。女店主会坐着缝衣服，钟摆的节拍填满安静的小屋。她喜欢那声音，还会顺便检查身旁的老缝纫机。墙上她给每一张完成的订单都留一道记号。有顾客进来，她就开一张收据，谢过人家照顾生意。她的那只小兔子睡在门边的箱子里。一天傍晚，一只小虫在她胳膊上咬了一口。她笑了笑，贴上创可贴，又回到钟那边去了。"},"trim":{"tw":[["cut",2],["top",3],["balance",2],["slash",6],["dress",3],["thin",5],["add",6],["clip",0]],"en":"Every spring my father would trim the tall hedge along the front wall. He used a sharp pair of shears to cut and clip the top into a level line. He liked to balance the two sides so they looked even. A single slash of the blade could spoil a whole afternoon's work. My sister would dress the small bushes with a thin rope to keep them straight. Then he would add a little water and stand back to look. In summer the garden was the pride of the street. He said patience, not strength, did the real job.","zh":"每年春天，父亲都会修剪前墙那一排高树篱。他用一把快剪把顶部剪得齐齐整整。他喜欢让两边保持均衡，看上去对称。刀锋只要斜斜一挥，就可能毁掉一下午的活儿。妹妹会用一根细绳把几丛小灌木拢直。然后他会添一点水，退后两步看看。夏天里，这个园子是整条街的骄傲。他说，干这活靠的是耐心，不是力气。"},"tuck":{"tw":[["gather",0],["dart",3],["position",2],["nip",6],["insert",0],["fold",2],["pillow",6],["pucker",0]],"en":"On Friday evening my mother began to tuck clean sheets around the spare bed. She would gather the corners and fold the top edge into a neat line. A small guest pillow lay on the chair, and she gave it a quick shake. To insert the fresh cover, she had to lift the heavy end alone. Her needle would nip a loose thread and hold it in position. 'Do not let the cloth pucker,' she said, as I watched from the door. Then she would dart to the kitchen and back with a warm blanket. By nine the room was ready, and it smelled of soap.","zh":"周五傍晚，母亲开始给备用客床掖好干净床单。她会把四个角收拢，把上边折成一道整齐的线。一只客人用的小枕头搁在椅子上，她拿起来抖了抖。要套上新的枕套，她得一个人抬起沉的那头。她的针会夹住一根松线，把它固定在合适的位置。她说，'别让布起皱，'我就在门口看着。然后她又会飞快地跑去厨房，抱回一条暖毯子。到九点，屋子收拾好了，闻着一股肥皂香。"},"upgrade":{"tw":[["climb",0],["prefer",3],["better",2],["provide",6],["raise",0],["rate",2],["improve",6],["rise",0]],"en":"Last month the manager decided to upgrade every old computer in our office. He would rather provide good tools than let the work slow down. I did not prefer the cheapest model, and I said so at the meeting. The new machines could improve the way we check each order. With faster screens, our rate of mistakes began to fall. Slowly the mood in the room seemed to rise and the complaints grew fewer. The chair asked for a small raise for the whole team. He said things were better now, but we could still climb higher.","zh":"上个月，经理决定给我们办公室每台旧电脑都升个级。他宁愿用好工具，也不愿让工作慢下来。我并不偏好最便宜的那款，会上也说了。新机器能改善我们核对每一份订单的方式。屏幕快了之后，我们出错的比率开始下降。屋里的气氛慢慢往好里走，抱怨也少了。主任替整个小组申请了一次小幅加薪。他说，现在情况好些了，可我们还能再往上爬。"},"verify":{"tw":[["control",0],["check",3],["test",2],["ascertain",6],["avow",0],["hold",3],["confirm",2],["specify",6]],"en":"In the school lab we had to verify the quality of a water sample from the river. The teacher asked us to check the colour first, then to test the acid level. We would hold the flask steady and control the heat so the glass did not crack. To ascertain the result, we ran the same test three times. My partner had to avow that no one had touched the bottle. We wrote down each number and asked the teacher to confirm it. She told us to specify the exact time of every step. In the end the sample was clean, and we felt proud.","zh":"在学校实验室里，我们得检验一份从河里取来的水样。老师让我们先看颜色，再测酸度。我们会握住烧瓶稳住它，并控制温度，别让玻璃裂开。为了弄清结果，我们把同样的测试做了三遍。我的搭档必须声明没人碰过那只瓶子。我们把每个数字记下来，请老师确认。她让我们把每一步的确切时间都写清楚。最后水样是干净的，我们都很自豪。"},"weary":{"tw":[["tire",0],["exhaust",3],["devolve",2],["impatient",6],["wear",0],["retire",3],["jaded",6],["fatigue",0]],"en":"After a long night shift the nurse looked weary but steady on her feet. The endless calls began to tire her, and the long night would exhaust her body. Her heavy shoes would wear out every few months on these hard floors. She could no longer hide a small sigh when a patient grew impatient. The hardest work often seemed to devolve to the youngest ones. When the older sister chose to retire, the ward lost its calm. Now everyone looked jaded and full of fatigue after a week of short sleep. Still, she stayed until the last light came up.","zh":"上了一整夜的班，那位护士看着很疲惫，脚下却还稳。没完没了的呼叫开始让她乏力，漫漫长夜又把她的身体掏空。在这硬邦邦的地板上，她沉甸甸的鞋几个月就得换一双。病人一不耐烦，她连一声轻叹都藏不住了。最累的活往往像是落到了最年轻的人身上。年长的那位姐姐一退休，病房就没了那份稳当。如今大家睡了一周短觉，都显得又倦又乏。可她还是留到最后一缕光升起。"},"script":{"tw":[["book",0],["dialogue",3],["write",2],["phrase",6],["hand",0],["scenario",3],["text",6]],"en":"The small theatre group had to learn a new script in only ten days. My sister would write her own lines in a thin book. The dialogue felt strange at first, and one long phrase kept failing her. The director asked her to read the text again in her own hand, slowly. In the final scenario her character had to leave the stage without a word. We practised that scene ten times. On the last night her voice did not shake. The audience clapped, and she forgot the fear completely.","zh":"这个小剧团只用了十天就要学会一部新剧本。我妹妹把她的台词写在一个薄本子上。那些对话一开始很别扭，有一个长句她老是念不顺。导演让她放慢，用自己的笔迹把文本再抄一遍。在最后的那个情景里，她的角色得一句话不说就退场。这场戏我们练了十遍。最后一晚，她的声音没有发抖。观众鼓了掌，她把害怕彻底忘了。"},"simulate":{"tw":[["assume",0],["play",3],["detect",6],["model",3],["mock",3],["technique",6],["imitate",0]],"en":"Before the bridge was built, engineers used a computer to simulate heavy traffic. They would assume that a thousand cars crossed it each hour. Their model could detect a weak point long before any real test. The technique saved both time and money. In a mock trial on screen, they let water imitate the weight of a full load. One young engineer said the program could play any weather they chose. For a moment the whole plan seemed real. Then they built the bridge, and it has held for years.","zh":"在桥建起来之前，工程师用电脑模拟了繁忙的交通。他们假设每小时有一千辆车过桥。他们的模型能在真正的测试之前很久就查出一个薄弱点。这项技术省了时间也省了钱。在屏幕上的一次假想试验里，他们让水来模仿满载的重量。有位年轻工程师说，这个程序能演出他们想要的任何一种天气。那一瞬，整个方案像是真的了。后来他们真的把桥建了起来，至今稳稳当当。"},"slam":{"tw":[["dig",0],["close",2],["round",6],["bang",0],["dance",2],["final",6],["sweep",0]],"en":"When my brother lost the game, he did not mean to slam the door. The bang still shook the whole house. My mother came out of the kitchen and asked him to sweep the step and then close it quietly. He went to dig in the garden for an hour to cool down. That evening the family had a round of cards, and the mood slowly changed. Nobody could dance well, but we all tried. In the final game he won and laughed again. Then he shut the door with two soft hands.","zh":"我弟弟输了那场游戏，他并不是故意把门摔上的。那声响还是震动了整座房子。我母亲从厨房出来，让他把台阶扫一下，再把门轻轻关上。他到园子里挖了一个钟头的土，好让气消下去。那天晚上家里打了一圈牌，气氛慢慢变了。谁也不会跳舞，可我们都试了。最后一局他赢了，又笑了起来。然后他用两只手轻轻把门关上。"},"slump":{"tw":[["correct",0],["drop",2],["recession",6],["sink",0],["collapse",2],["plunge",6],["decline",0]],"en":"Sales at the small shop began to slump in the second year. The owner watched each number drop and could not correct the trend in time. A long recession in the town made every customer careful with money. Prices continued to decline, yet few people came to buy. He saw his savings sink with the failing business. A single bad month could make the whole shop collapse. In winter the trade took a sudden plunge, and he closed one room. By spring he had a smaller shop and a calmer life.","zh":"那家小店第二年销量开始下滑。店主眼看着每个数字往下掉，却没能及时改正这个势头。镇上持续很久的不景气让每个顾客都攥紧了钱。价格一路走低，来买的人却很少。他看着自己的积蓄跟着生意一起沉下去。一个糟糕的月份就可能让整家店垮掉。到了冬天，生意猛地暴跌，他关掉了一间店面。到春天，他的店小了，日子反倒清静了。"},"soar":{"tw":[["surge",0],["billow",3],["fly",2],["plummet",6],["zoom",0],["rise",2],["plunge",6]],"en":"After the forest was protected, the number of eagles began to soar. A sharp surge in the bird count surprised the whole region. On windy days their wings would billow like dark cloth over the valley. Visitors came to watch them fly above the river. In one cold week the count seemed to plummet when the fish moved away. The next spring it began to rise again. A young guide would zoom in with her camera and count each nest. One hard plunge after a fish was the best thing we saw all day.","zh":"森林受到保护之后，雕的数量开始猛增。鸟的数量一下子涨了这么多，让整个地区都很惊讶。起风的日子，它们的翅膀像一块块深色的布在山谷上翻卷。游客们来看它们在河上飞。有一周天冷，鱼游走了，数量好像骤然下跌。第二年春天，数字又开始上升。一位年轻向导会用相机拉近镜头，数每一个巢。一次朝鱼猛冲下去的扑击，是我们那天看到的最精彩的一幕。"},"span":{"tw":[["couple",0],["cover",2],["length",6],["cross",0],["motion",2],["wide",6],["pair",0]],"en":"The old stone bridge has a span of almost forty metres across the river. A couple of workers built its first arch by hand two hundred years ago. The full length of the road there can cover three small fields. To cross the water, carts had to climb a wide, gentle slope. Every motion of the heavy wheels was slow and careful. A pair of stone lions still stands at each end. My grandfather used to tell me the story on our walks. He said good work outlives the people who make it.","zh":"那座老石桥横跨河面，跨度将近四十米。两百年前，两个工人用手砌出了它的第一道拱。那段路全长能盖住三块小田。要过河，大车得爬上一道又宽又缓的坡。沉重的车轮每动一下都又慢又小心。两头至今还各立着一对石狮子。我爷爷以前散步时总给我讲这个故事。他说，干得好的活儿，比做它的人活得更久。"},"spark":{"tw":[["light",0],["flash",2],["ignite",6],["trip",0],["trace",2],["wave",6],["discharge",0]],"en":"One small spark from a cut wire was enough to ignite the dry grass near the factory. A bright flash followed, and then a thin line of smoke. The night guard saw the light from his window and ran outside. He had to trip the main switch before the fire could spread. Later, engineers found a clear trace of heat along the cable. They said a sudden discharge had burned the cover away. A wave of hot air had moved across the yard in seconds. Now every line is checked twice a year.","zh":"一根被割破的电线上迸出的一点小火花，就足以把厂子附近的干草点着。紧接着是一道亮光，然后是一缕细细的烟。守夜的人从窗户里看见了火光，跑了出去。他得在火蔓延开之前扳下总闸。后来，工程师在电缆上找到了一道明显的过热痕迹。他们说，是一次突然的放电把外皮烧掉了。一股热浪几秒钟就扫过了整个院子。如今每条线路一年查两次。"},"spice":{"tw":[["zest",0],["salt",3],["change",2],["sweet",6],["ginger",3],["season",2],["taste",6]],"en":"My grandmother said that one good spice can change a whole pot of soup. She would add a little ginger and a small amount of salt. A sweet taste was never enough for her; she wanted something sharper. The zest of a lemon gave the dish a fresh note. Each season she cooked the same soup in a slightly different way. We children learned to taste before we spoke. Her food always had a little heat and a lot of care. Nobody in the family has ever copied it exactly.","zh":"我奶奶说，一样好香料就能改变一整锅汤。她会放一点姜和一小撮盐。光有甜味从来不能满足她；她想要更冲一点的味道。一片柠檬皮给这道菜添了一股清新的气息。每到一个季节，她煮同一锅汤的法子都会略有不同。我们这些孩子学会了先尝再说话。她做的菜总带着一点辣和很多心思。家里谁也没能把它照原样做出来。"},"spur":{"tw":[["spine",0],["line",2],["gap",6],["prod",0],["strike",2],["push",6],["goad",0]],"en":"The coach knew how to spur a tired team into one last effort. He would prod them with a simple question and then wait. His sharp words could goad a runner past her own limit. A long line of small stones marked the course for the race. At the steep gap in the path he stood and called out the time. That push was enough to make us strike the final hill hard. He always said a straight spine wins more races than strong legs. We finished third, but we ran better than ever.","zh":"教练知道怎么鞭策一支疲惫的队伍再拼最后一次。他会用一个简单的问题戳一戳他们，然后等着。他尖刻的话能把一个跑者激过自己的极限。一排小石子标出了赛跑的路线。在路上一处陡峭的缺口旁，他站着喊时间。那一推，足够让我们狠狠地冲向最后一道坡。他总说，挺直的脊背比强壮的双腿能赢下更多的比赛。我们跑了第三，却跑出了前所未有的水平。"},"stagger":{"tw":[["stumble",0],["walk",2],["hobble",6],["reel",0],["overwhelm",2],["trundle",6],["lurch",0]],"en":"After two nights without sleep, the young nurse began to stagger in the corridor. She would stumble on the smooth floor and then walk very slowly. A pain in her knee made her hobble past the last room. Her head would reel whenever she stopped to think. A cart with breakfast would trundle by, and she had to wait. The tiredness began to overwhelm her, and the floor seemed to lurch under her feet. The head nurse sent her home at once. She slept for twelve hours and came back steady.","zh":"连着两夜没睡之后，那位年轻护士在走廊里开始摇摇晃晃。她会在地板上绊一下，然后走得很慢。膝盖的疼让她一瘸一拐地走过最后一个房间。只要一停下来想事，她的头就发晕。送早饭的车会嘎吱嘎吱地推过去，她只好等着。疲倦开始把她压垮，脚下的地板似乎也在晃。护士长立刻让她回家。她睡了十二个小时，回来时稳稳当当。"},"stitch":{"tw":[["sew",0],["gather",3],["pain",2],["weave",6],["tick",3],["fasten",2],["thread",6]],"en":"The nurse had to put a small stitch in the cut on my hand. She told me to sit still and to fasten my eyes on the wall. I felt one short pain when the needle went in, then nothing. At home my mother would sew cloth and weave baskets in the same chair. She showed me how to gather the loose thread and tie it. A clock on the shelf would tick through the whole afternoon. That quiet sound made the work easier. By evening my hand was clean and closed.","zh":"护士得在我手上的伤口上缝一针。她让我坐好，把眼睛盯在墙上。针扎进去时有一阵短短的疼，接着就没事了。在家里，我母亲会在同一把椅子上缝布、编篮子。她教我怎样把松了的线收起来打上结。架上的一只钟会滴答滴答响一整个下午。那静静的声音让干活轻松了些。到傍晚，我的手已经干干净净地合上了。"},"straw":{"tw":[["stalk",0],["litter",3],["cover",2],["rice",6],["husk",0],["yellow",2],["white",6]],"en":"In the late summer the field was full of dry yellow straw after the harvest. My uncle would cut each stalk and let it fall in long lines. He used the dry straw to litter the floor of the animal shed. In winter a thick cover of it kept the young animals warm. A bag of rice and a pile of husk sat in the corner of the barn. The white smoke from the fire rose over the roof. He said nothing on a farm is wasted. The smallest seed can feed a family in the cold months.","zh":"盛夏过去了，收割后的田里满是干黄的稻草。我叔叔把每一根秸秆割下来，让它们排成长长的一行行。他用干草给牲口棚的地面垫窝。到了冬天，厚厚一层草让幼畜暖和。谷仓角落里放着一袋米和一堆谷壳。白色的炊烟从屋顶升起来。他说，在农场上没有一样东西是白费的。最小的一粒种子，也能在冷天里养活一家人。"},"stride":{"tw":[["step",2],["walk",2],["swing",6],["pace",0],["traverse",2],["bounce",6],["tread",0]],"en":"My father has a long stride that makes him hard to follow on a hill, even when the path is clear. Each step of his is almost twice the length of mine. He will walk ahead and never look back, so I have to hurry to keep up. His arms swing as he goes, easy and steady. On the flat ground we keep the same pace for hours without speaking. Together we traverse the whole ridge before noon. He likes to bounce over small stones instead of going round them. 'Watch where you tread,' he says, 'and the mountain will be kind.'","zh":"我父亲步子迈得很大，在山上跟着他很难。他每一步几乎是我的两倍长。他会走在前面，从不回头。走起来两条胳膊自然摆动，又轻松又稳。在平地上，我们能保持同样的速度走上好几个钟头。我们俩一起在中午之前走完了整道山脊。碰到小石头，他喜欢蹦过去，而不是绕开。他说，'看准脚下踩的地方，山就会对你客气。'"},"stroll":{"tw":[["promenade",0],["ramble",3],["walk",2],["wander",6],["amble",0],["jaunt",6],["saunter",0]],"en":"After dinner my aunt and I took a slow stroll along the wide promenade beside the sea. She likes to amble and look at every shop window. On the way we would wander into a small square to hear a street band. A short jaunt like that can make a whole evening feel new. We let the children ramble ahead and did not hurry after them. Two old men passed us at a quick walk, talking about the news. My aunt could saunter for hours and never say she was tired. We came home after dark and slept well.","zh":"晚饭后，我和姑妈沿着海边宽阔的散步道慢慢溜达。她喜欢不紧不慢地走，看每一家商店的橱窗。路上我们会拐进一个小广场，听街头乐队演奏。像这样出去转一小圈，就能让整个晚上变得新鲜。我们让孩子们在前面乱跑，也不急着追。两个老人快步从我们身边走过，聊着新闻。我姑妈能悠闲地走好几个钟头，从不说累。天黑后我们回到家，睡得很好。"},"stumble":{"tw":[["hit",0],["move",2],["fade",6],["trip",0],["walk",2],["haunt",6],["stagger",0]],"en":"On the icy path outside my door I watched a neighbour stumble and almost fall. He took a hard trip on a loose stone, but he did not go down. He tried to walk on, and then his shoulder hit the wall. The pain made him stagger for a moment. He did not move for a while and then laughed at himself. A thin patch of ice would fade as the sun came up. He said the same corner had been a haunt of accidents for years. I took his arm and we went inside for tea, walking slowly.","zh":"在门前结冰的小路上，我看见一位邻居绊了一下，差点摔倒。他被一块松石头狠狠绊了一跤，却没有倒下。他想继续往前走，肩膀却撞到了墙上。那一疼让他晃了一下。他好一会儿没动，然后自嘲地笑了。太阳一出来，薄薄的一层冰就会化掉。他说这个拐角多年来一直是出事的地方。我扶着他的胳膊，我们一起进屋喝茶，走得很慢。"},"subscribe":{"tw":[["sign",0],["agree",2],["publish",6],["support",0],["buy",2],["advertise",6],["pledge",0]],"en":"Last winter I decided to subscribe to a monthly magazine about small machines. I had to sign a short form online and agree to pay for one year. The editor would publish a new issue every month. I chose to support the paper because its writers test every device they write about. It was cheaper to buy the yearly plan than to pay each time. Companies pay a lot to advertise in those pages, which keeps the price low. I also made a pledge to read it before I bought anything new. So far I have kept that promise.","zh":"去年冬天，我决定订阅一本关于小型机械的月刊。我不得不在网上签一份短表，并同意付一年的钱。编辑每个月都会出一期。我选择支持这份刊物，因为它的作者会试用自己写到的每一件设备。买全年比每次单买便宜。有些公司花大价钱在那几页上做广告，这也压低了价格。我还下过一个决心：买新东西之前先把刊物读完。到目前为止，这个诺言我还守着。"},"subsidiary":{"tw":[["subordinate",0],["man",3],["company",2],["conglomerate",6],["auxiliary",0],["associate",3],["venture",6]],"en":"The company I work for is a subsidiary of a large group that owns shops in six regions. My first job there was subordinate to the head of the design office. A man with a quiet voice ran the whole department from a small room. The parent conglomerate bought our firm three years ago and changed little at first. We were an auxiliary team that helped the main office with new products. An associate from another city joined us in spring for a joint venture. Together we opened a new line of simple tools. The name on our door is still the same.","zh":"我所在的公司，是一个在六个地区都有店铺的大集团的子公司。我在那儿的第一份工作，是听设计室主任的调遣。一个声音很轻的男人在一间小屋里管着整个部门。三年前，母公司买下了我们这家公司，起初改动很小。我们是一支辅助团队，帮总部做新产品。春天，一位来自另一座城市的合伙人加入进来，一起做合资的项目。我们合力推出了一条简易工具的新产品线。门口的名字到现在还没变。"},"surge":{"tw":[["rush",0],["better",2],["decline",6],["tide",0],["rise",2],["drop",6],["soar",0]],"en":"At high tide a sudden surge of water pushed over the low wall of the harbor. The rush carried small boats against the steps and broke two ropes. Fishermen said the level would rise for another hour before it began to decline. Then the wind dropped and the sea grew calm again. Numbers of visitors to the coast would soar in the warm months, but that week the roads were empty. The old boat needed better repairs than anyone had thought. In the morning we found sand and broken wood all along the street. Nobody had been hurt.","zh":"涨潮时，一股突如其来的涌流翻过了海港的低墙。那股急流把小船冲到台阶上，撞断了两根缆绳。渔民们说，水位还会再涨一个钟头，然后才开始回落。接着风停了，海面又平静下来。天暖的时候，来海边的游客数量会猛增，可那一周路上空空的。那条旧船需要比大家想的更好的修补。早上，我们发现整条街都是沙子和碎木头。没有人受伤。"},"textile":{"tw":[["cloth",0],["elastic",3],["export",6],["material",0],["satin",3],["cement",6],["fabric",4]],"en":"In the old mill on the river, workers once made textile for the whole region. Every kind of cloth was woven there, from rough working fabric to fine satin. A long strip of elastic material was packed into rolls and sent abroad. The export trade grew for twenty years and then stopped. When the mill closed, a cement wall was built across the loading yard. Only the smell of oil and dust remained. My grandfather kept one small square of cloth in a wooden box. He said the town had been rich because of that thin cotton.","zh":"在河边那座老纺织厂里，工人们曾经为整个地区织布。那里织过各种各样的布，从粗糙的工作布到细密的缎子。一条条有弹性的料子卷成筒，运往国外。这项出口生意红火了二十年，然后停了。厂子关门后，装货的院子里砌起了一堵水泥墙。只剩下机油和灰尘的气味。我爷爷在木盒子里留着一小块布。他说，这座镇子曾经因为那种薄薄的棉布而富裕过。"},"thumb":{"tw":[["finger",2],["ride",2],["shoulder",6],["flip",0],["touch",2],["sore",6],["flick",0]],"en":"While fixing the chain on his bike, my cousin hurt his thumb. He could not move the small part with any finger of his right hand. So he asked me to ride the bike home for him. I had to flip the chain back with a screwdriver and a quick flick of the wrist. The work put a sore feeling in my shoulder as well. Every time I touch the metal, a sharp note runs up my arm. He watched and gave advice from the wall. In the end the chain was fine, and his thumb only needed rest.","zh":"我表哥修自行车链条的时候伤了拇指。他右手任何一根手指都动不了那个小零件。于是他让我替他把车骑回家。我只好用一把螺丝刀，手腕一抖，把链条翻回去。这活也让我肩膀酸疼起来。每次我碰到那块金属，一阵刺痛就顺着手臂上来。他靠在墙边看着，出主意。最后链条没事了，他的拇指只需要休息。"},"thunder":{"tw":[["boom",0],["move",2],["rumble",6],["roar",2],["noise",2],["lightning",6],["smack",0]],"en":"A storm came over the valley in the night, and the thunder woke every house. The first boom shook the windows, and the walls seemed to move. A long rumble followed, low and slow, like a heavy cart on a stone road. Then a white line of lightning lit the whole field. The roar of the rain on the roof made any other noise impossible to hear. One flash came so near that it sounded like a smack on the glass. My sister and I sat on the floor and waited. By morning the sky was clean and quiet.","zh":"夜里，一场暴风雨越过山谷，雷声把家家户户都吵醒了。第一声轰响震得窗户直响，墙似乎也在动。接着是一阵长长的低鸣，又低又慢，像大车碾过石头路。然后一道白色的闪电照亮了整片田野。雨水砸在屋顶上的轰鸣，让别的什么声音都听不见。有一道闪电离得很近，听上去像在玻璃上拍了一下。我和妹妹坐在地板上等。到早上，天空干干净净、安安静静。"},"transplant":{"tw":[["transfer",0],["shift",2],["liver",6],["graft",0],["insert",2],["patient",6],["transpose",0]],"en":"The hospital had to transplant a small part of a liver into a very sick patient. Doctors would first transfer the tissue from one room to another in a cold box. Then they had to shift the plan when the patient's fever rose. The graft had to be perfect, because a poor one can fail in hours. They would insert a thin tube to help the blood flow and transpose two small veins. The surgery lasted all night. By dawn the patient was stable and breathing alone. His family thanked the team in the hall, softly.","zh":"医院得把一小块肝脏移植到一位病得很重的病人身上。医生要先把组织装在冷藏箱里，从一个房间转到另一个房间。接着，病人的体温升上来，他们只好改变方案。这块移植物必须完美，因为差一点的就可能在几个小时内失败。他们要插入一根细管帮血液流通，还要把两根小血管换个位置。手术做了一整夜。到天亮时，病人情况稳定，能自己呼吸了。他的家人在走廊里轻声道谢。"},"tremble":{"tw":[["shake",2],["shudder",3],["reflex",2],["weep",6],["shiver",0],["quiver",3],["caress",6]],"en":"When my grandmother read the old letter, her hands began to tremble. She would shake her head and then read the same line again. A cold shiver ran through her, though the room was warm, and she could not stop it. Such a shudder was a simple reflex of memory, she said, not of cold. She tried not to weep in front of us. I saw the paper quiver in her fingers. She let me caress her hand until the shaking stopped. Then she folded the letter and put it back in the box.","zh":"我奶奶读那封旧信时，两只手开始发抖。她摇摇头，又把同一行再读一遍。屋里明明是暖的，她却打了个冷战，怎么也停不下来。她说，这样的战栗只是回忆的一种本能反应，不是因为冷。她尽量不在我们面前哭。我看见那张纸在她指间微微颤动。她让我轻轻抚着她的手，直到抖动停下。然后她把信折好，放回了盒子里。"},"tug":{"tw":[["drive",0],["boat",2],["submarine",6],["push",0],["fight",2],["ship",6],["labour",0]],"en":"A small boat had to tug a broken ship back to the harbor before the storm. The captain would drive the engine hard and push against the wind. It was a slow fight against the tide and the heavy load. Every metre of the way took real labour from the crew. Once a grey submarine passed us on its way out to sea. One sailor stood at the rail and waved. The rope held, and the two boats came in together. We watched from the shore and felt proud of them.","zh":"一条小船得在暴风雨来之前，把一艘坏了的轮船拖回海港。船长把发动机开得很猛，顶着风往前推。这是跟潮水与重载的一场慢仗。每一米路，都要船员付出实实在在的力气。有一次，一艘灰色的潜艇出海时从我们旁边驶过。一个水手站在栏杆边挥了挥手。缆绳撑住了，两条船一起进了港。我们在岸上看着，为他们感到骄傲。"},"worship":{"tw":[["revere",0],["offer",3],["love",2],["religious",6],["praise",3],["attend",2],["holy",6]],"en":"On a quiet Sunday morning people came to worship in the old stone hall. They would attend the service and offer a few coins for the poor. The building is not large, but many call it holy ground. A young teacher said she had learned to revere the silence inside more than the walls. Her religious life, she explained, was mostly about care for others. Neighbours praised her for the food she gave away each week. Some of that work came from love, not from duty. After the last song, everyone walked home under the trees.","zh":"一个安静的星期天早上，人们来到那座石头老厅里做礼拜。他们会参加礼拜，为穷人捐几个硬币。这建筑不大，可许多人称它是圣地。一位年轻教师说，她学会了敬重里面那份安静，胜过敬重这些墙。她解释说，她的宗教生活多半就是关心别人。邻居们都夸她每周送出去的食物。那些事有些出于爱，而不是出于义务。最后一支歌唱完，大家沿着树荫走回家。"}}});
